<node>

    <node name="name" channel="inline" format="text/plain" model="Watchdog System - Server Activity Viewer"/>
    <node name="description" channel="inline" format="text/plain" model="Beobachten von Server-Aktivität and Antwortverhalten"/>
    <node name="technology" channel="inline" format="text/plain" model="(beliebig; Web-basiert)"/>
    <node name="licence" channel="inline" format="text/plain" model="GNU GPL, GNU FDL"/>
    <node name="portal" channel="inline" format="text/plain" model=""/>
    <node name="contact" channel="inline" format="text/plain" model="Administrator: Herr Martin Schulz"/>
    <node name="remark" channel="inline" format="text/plain" model="The administration department of the University of Cooperative Education Leipzig needs a tool to observe server activity and responsiveness. A necessary first step will be the analysis of the problem domain. Existing watchdog systems are to be investigated closely (functionality, programming language used, architecture, frontend/ user interface etc.). Afterwards, Mr. Aschmann should be consulted to introduce the results of the investigation and ask for further requirements. All results have to be written down in a technical specification document (Pflichtenheft), supported by suitable Unified Modeling Language (UML) diagrams, e.g. the Deployment Diagram (DD). But also non-UML diagrams like the Network Diagram (ND) are allowed. Depending on the results of the first step of this project, either a new application is to be implemented as prototype, or an existing Free/ Open Source Software (FOSS) application extended with additional functionality. Hereby, the user interface should be kept as simple and intuitive as possible."/>

</node>
